From: tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:55:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: nvmem: describe Apple Broadcom OTP module
 identity

Describe the dynamic vendor identity field shared by the Wi-Fi and Bluetooth functions of Apple radio modules.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../nvmem/layouts/brcm,apple-otp-layout.yaml  | 43 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/brcm,apple-otp-layout.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/brcm,apple-otp-layout.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/brcm,apple-otp-layout.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..f2a5c1f53
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/brcm,apple-otp-layout.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/nvmem/layouts/brcm,apple-otp-layout.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Apple module identity layout in Broadcom radio OTP
+
+maintainers:
+  - tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
+
+description:
+  Apple Broadcom radio modules contain type-length-value OTP records. The
+  SYS_VENDOR record includes a chip-parameter string and a board-parameter
+  string after a four-byte header. The board parameters identify the module
+  vendor in a V= field. Its position is discovered from the record contents,
+  not a fixed byte offset. A shared Bluetooth radio uses this identity to
+  select its matching firmware. The provider supplies the raw record region
+  beginning with the first type byte, rather than the entire OTP address space.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: brcm,apple-otp-layout
+
+  module-vendor:
+    type: object
+    description: Module vendor string, without the V= prefix or terminator.
+    additionalProperties: false
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - module-vendor
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    nvmem-layout {
+        compatible = "brcm,apple-otp-layout";
+
+        module_vendor: module-vendor {
+        };
+    };
